"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nIt was the first cafe I visited right after arriving in Australia.  \nIt was my first coffee on unfamiliar Melbourne soil, and it turned out to be the best coffee of my entire trip — perfectly suited to my taste.  \n\nThe  of the owner who took my order was surprisingly right up my alley.  \nSeeing the  the owner was wearing and the cafe name — a combination of chemical element symbols (Ca, Fe, In) — I was convinced he had an engineering background.  \n\nHe was friendly yet clearly took great pride in his coffee.  \nThanks to him, my very first impression of Australia remained a warm and wonderful memory.  \n\n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n"